Day 30: Database Selection & Design Review  

Topic:  
Exploration of database selection criteria and design principles, including the CAP theorem, to determine the most suitable database for specific business scenarios.  

Learning Objectives:  

• Understand how to choose the right database based on problem requirements.  
• Learn the basics of the CAP theorem (Consistency, Availability, Partition Tolerance).  
• Apply knowledge to justify database selection for real-world business scenarios.  

Activities / Deliverables:  

• Analyze three Volyo business scenarios and recommend the appropriate database.  
• Create a presentation justifying database choices.  
• Review and compare MySQL, PostgreSQL, and SQLite for specific use cases.  

Important Concepts:  

• CAP theorem: Trade-offs between Consistency, Availability, and Partition Tolerance.  
• Factors influencing database selection: scalability, performance, data complexity, and use case.  

SQL Syntax / Commands:  

• N/A (Conceptual focus, no specific SQL commands).  

Real-world Use Cases:  

• Selecting PostgreSQL for complex transactional systems.  
• Choosing SQLite for lightweight, embedded applications.  
• Opting for MySQL for web applications requiring fast read operations.  

Tools / Tech:  

• MySQL, PostgreSQL, SQLite.  
• Presentation software (e.g., MS PowerPoint).  

Summary:  
Learned to evaluate database options based on business requirements and the CAP theorem. Applied this knowledge to select the most suitable database for Volyo scenarios, reinforcing database design principles.  

